WEBVTT

00:00:59.685 --> 00:01:01.103
[woman speaking Mandarin]

00:01:04.857 --> 00:01:06.692
[speaking English]
She says it is the work...

00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:08.611
of the barbarian devil king.

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:12.239
[speaking Mandarin]

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.243
[man speaking English]
Her village

00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:19.747
was loyal to the rebel Song dynasty.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.290
If one does not submit
to the rule of the Khan...

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:25.043
this is what happens.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:29.589
[whimpering]

00:01:42.019 --> 00:01:45.063
[speaking Mongolian]

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.567
[Maffeo] Gerege!

00:01:49.652 --> 00:01:50.653
[shouting orders]

00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:28.982
[indistinct chatter]

00:02:57.219 --> 00:02:59.179
[man shouting in foreign language]

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:01.348
[door creaking]

00:04:07.122 --> 00:04:08.749
[speaking foreign language]

00:04:18.425 --> 00:04:20.093
[Kublai speaking English]
The Latins.

00:04:20.177 --> 00:04:22.345
Yes, I remember.

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:24.932
But where are the Christian priests
you were to bring, hmm?

00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:29.227
[Niccolò] Lord Kublai...
please accept our remorse.

00:04:29.311 --> 00:04:32.773
Our priests could not bear
the rigors of the journey.

00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:36.484
But we did bring you holy oil from--

00:04:36.568 --> 00:04:40.280
Your men of God retreat,
but this boy advances.

00:04:40.363 --> 00:04:42.740
It says very little for your savior.
Hmm?

00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:43.867
[court murmuring]

00:04:45.035 --> 00:04:49.497
Loyalty... of a mortal son
to a mortal father, Great Khan.

00:04:49.581 --> 00:04:50.707
Hmm.

00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:53.585
Holy oil

00:04:53.668 --> 00:04:55.503
from the pontiff
who wishes to spread

00:04:55.587 --> 00:04:58.340
Christianity throughout my lands.

00:04:58.423 --> 00:05:02.302
Is this not the same Pope
who has called me "the spawn of Satan"?

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:06.514
I will say this and you will listen.

00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:10.393
Christianity is welcome in my kingdom.

00:05:10.477 --> 00:05:12.020
As is Buddhism...

00:05:12.104 --> 00:05:15.690
Judaism...
Islam...

00:05:15.773 --> 00:05:20.445
and the Eternal Blue Sky
of my grandfather, Genghis Khan,

00:05:20.528 --> 00:05:23.115
descended from a wolf.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:39.672
So, tell your Pope
that he himself must bow before me...

00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:42.050
and pledge his fealty to me.

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:44.302
As for you merchants...

00:05:44.386 --> 00:05:47.555
you crossed ocean and mountain...

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:50.600
the great Takla Makan Desert.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.810
One not many men survive.

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:57.274
Describe for me my desert, hmm?

00:06:00.777 --> 00:06:02.279
It is a...

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:05.573
most barren region, Sire.

00:06:06.241 --> 00:06:09.119
No water. No life, Lord Khan.

00:06:09.744 --> 00:06:13.123
-Not even a bird.
-Not even a bird.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.334
It is, Great Khan...
a sea of death.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:21.798
Yet very much alive.

00:06:23.675 --> 00:06:24.801
At night you hear it.

00:06:26.094 --> 00:06:29.932
The shifting sands, they... sing.

00:06:30.015 --> 00:06:31.141
Humble apologies, Sire.

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:34.019
-He does not yet know the rules of the--
-[Kublai grunts]

00:06:35.687 --> 00:06:37.355
Continue.

00:06:39.983 --> 00:06:43.653
Voices like... spirits...

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:47.532
trying to lure you off course.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.535
This is why men die out there.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.288
The Uighurs called it...

00:06:53.371 --> 00:06:56.083
[speaking foreign language]

00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:58.543
You learned the tongue of the Uighurs?

00:06:58.626 --> 00:07:01.629
Three years was not long enough
to learn it all.

00:07:02.589 --> 00:07:03.590
[speaking Mongolian]

00:07:03.673 --> 00:07:05.508
[speaking Mongolian]

00:07:09.679 --> 00:07:11.056
[scoffs]

00:07:13.683 --> 00:07:14.935
[chuckles]

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:18.355
[speaking English] Of all the lands
a traveler passes through...

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:20.690
which province contains...

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:23.651
in your eye,
the most beautiful women of all?

00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:32.827
I find that all women,
no matter from which land...

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.663
they are all beautiful
in their own unique manner.

00:07:36.373 --> 00:07:38.500
In Italy, we have a saying...

00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:42.629
[speaking Italian]

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:46.799
[speaking English]
"The true sweetness of wine...

00:07:46.883 --> 00:07:49.011
is one flavor."

00:07:49.094 --> 00:07:51.429
[scattered laughter]

00:07:55.976 --> 00:07:57.227
[Kublai chuckling]

00:07:59.062 --> 00:08:00.730
You have a clever mind.

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:03.733
For a Latin.

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:06.653
I made one request.
It was not for oil.

00:08:06.736 --> 00:08:10.073
It was for priests.
With this, you failed.

00:08:10.157 --> 00:08:11.283
Take your leave.

00:08:11.366 --> 00:08:13.243
Go, Latins.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:15.495
You're banished forever.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:22.710
You are most correct, Lord Khan.

00:08:22.794 --> 00:08:24.671
The boy...

00:08:24.754 --> 00:08:28.091
has a clever mind and...
excellent perception.

00:08:30.093 --> 00:08:31.553
He is my son...

00:08:33.805 --> 00:08:35.432
and most dear to me.

00:08:37.225 --> 00:08:40.770
But if it pleases Your Greatness,
you may take him as your man and servant.

00:08:43.315 --> 00:08:45.067
What do you wish in return?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:48.403
The opportunity to pay tribute
to my Khan from my journeys...

00:08:48.486 --> 00:08:50.363
along the Silk Road.

00:08:50.447 --> 00:08:51.989
Father, what are you doing?

00:08:52.074 --> 00:08:54.742
Marco, trust this. Be silent.

00:08:54.826 --> 00:08:57.162
-I am your son.
-[whispering] Be silent.

00:08:57.245 --> 00:09:01.333
You wish not the honor of service
in the court of the Khan of Khans?

00:09:04.336 --> 00:09:08.923
What greater tribute can a man offer
than his own flesh and his own blood?

00:09:11.008 --> 00:09:14.221
You Latin merchants
may engage in trade along my Silk Road.

00:09:14.304 --> 00:09:16.223
Ahmad, my Minister of Finance,

00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:18.350
will discuss taxation and transit.

00:09:18.433 --> 00:09:20.017
Take your leave.

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.063
-Marco, you have to trust me.
-Father!

00:09:23.146 --> 00:09:24.939
-This will not be forever.
-Don't do this.

00:09:25.022 --> 00:09:28.526
We will secure the trade routes
and be back for you.

00:09:31.654 --> 00:09:33.990
And I still want those priests.

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:37.244
Father!
Don't leave me here.

00:09:43.625 --> 00:09:45.585
[gasping]

00:09:59.807 --> 00:10:01.684
[guards speaking foreign language]

00:10:08.275 --> 00:10:10.277
[theme music playing]

00:11:51.919 --> 00:11:54.797
[conversing indistinctly]

00:12:13.941 --> 00:12:17.737
[Marco speaking Italian]

00:12:32.544 --> 00:12:34.796
-[bells tolling]
-[gulls squawking]

00:12:45.515 --> 00:12:49.143
[nun speaking Italian]

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.886
[speaking English] Of all the things
I expected to come home to

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:25.347
after all these years...

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.306
[sighs]

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:30.727
"Marco." She gave you a fine name.

00:13:36.107 --> 00:13:37.359
When did she pass?

00:13:40.695 --> 00:13:42.196
I was six.

00:13:52.707 --> 00:13:53.875
From Jerusalem.

00:13:54.792 --> 00:13:57.504
It has guarded my heart for 14 years.

00:14:01.799 --> 00:14:03.760
Psalms 72:11.

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:07.013
"All kings shall fall before him."

00:14:15.062 --> 00:14:17.649
-Where were you?
-The Silk Road.

00:14:18.775 --> 00:14:20.234
It ends here in Venezia.

00:14:20.317 --> 00:14:23.237
It stretches 4,000 miles
across the world.

00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:27.742
Why did you never
send word to Mother?

00:14:29.827 --> 00:14:31.829
It is not simple.

00:14:31.913 --> 00:14:34.457
We had an arrangement.

00:14:34.541 --> 00:14:38.586
But had I any idea
of the birth of a son...

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.510
You have her eyes.

00:14:48.471 --> 00:14:50.640
Well, now...

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:52.684
your Uncle Maffeo and I...

00:14:52.767 --> 00:14:54.602
we have important business
to discuss with the Bishop

00:14:54.686 --> 00:14:56.646
before we set sail again.

00:14:56.729 --> 00:14:59.065
[Marco] I will travel with you.

00:15:01.984 --> 00:15:06.030
Father.
Do not leave me alone again.

00:15:06.113 --> 00:15:07.574
This is not possible.

00:15:09.701 --> 00:15:13.037
You are not prepared
for the rigors of the journey ahead.

00:16:08.843 --> 00:16:11.638
-[wind howling]
-[priest] Lord, help us!

00:16:11.721 --> 00:16:13.556
Lord, help us!

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.224
Get over there!

00:16:16.726 --> 00:16:18.435
I can help!

00:16:19.687 --> 00:16:22.023
You defied me, boy!

00:16:22.106 --> 00:16:25.151
You do not belong here!
Stay away from me!

00:16:41.876 --> 00:16:44.003
[Marco speaking Farsi]

00:16:44.086 --> 00:16:45.588
[man speaking English]
No, no, no.

00:16:45.672 --> 00:16:47.882
[speaking Farsi]

00:16:47.965 --> 00:16:49.884
[repeats phrase in Farsi]

00:16:49.967 --> 00:16:50.968
[speaking English]
Very good.

00:16:51.052 --> 00:16:52.303
[laughs]

00:16:52.386 --> 00:16:55.890
[priest] This is not what we imagined.
We must return to our flock.

00:16:55.973 --> 00:16:58.142
You are not abandoning our factor.

00:16:58.225 --> 00:16:59.811
Your Bishop gave you orders.

00:16:59.894 --> 00:17:01.688
Then follow us back to Venice...

00:17:01.771 --> 00:17:03.397
and bring the Bishop instead.

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.942
Uncle, Uncle,
these are men of God.

00:17:07.985 --> 00:17:10.196
-Godspeed.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:17:10.279 --> 00:17:11.405
[Marco grunting]

00:17:15.993 --> 00:17:17.704
Enough!

00:17:17.787 --> 00:17:21.373
You have no knowledge of our world!
Do not act as if you do!

00:17:26.671 --> 00:17:27.714
Take your donkey.

00:17:27.797 --> 00:17:30.174
Follow the priests back to the ship.

00:17:31.133 --> 00:17:32.343
Go home.

00:18:05.835 --> 00:18:06.878
[Niccolò] Marco!

00:18:09.463 --> 00:18:10.590
Marco!

00:18:11.507 --> 00:18:15.052
-[Marco mumbling deliriously]
-[Niccolò shushing]

00:18:19.431 --> 00:18:21.308
[Maffeo] We have lost three days.

00:18:21.392 --> 00:18:22.977
[Niccolò] We haven't lost a thing, Maffeo.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:25.813
The Khan and our trade routes
slip away

00:18:25.897 --> 00:18:28.733
while you make amends
for your fatherly sins.

00:18:28.816 --> 00:18:30.985
He is our blood.

00:18:31.068 --> 00:18:32.153
Mark my words.

00:18:32.236 --> 00:18:35.281
He will gut the foundation of
everything we have labored to build.

00:18:36.407 --> 00:18:38.159
-Get out.
-What?

00:18:38.242 --> 00:18:40.161
Get out.

00:20:11.127 --> 00:20:13.170
[faint rumbling]

00:20:23.639 --> 00:20:24.640
Run!

00:20:24.724 --> 00:20:26.225
-[Maffeo] Take cover!
-Everyone, run!

00:20:26.308 --> 00:20:28.477
Run! Go!

00:20:29.645 --> 00:20:30.980
Go! Run!

00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:35.735
[Maffeo] Take cover!

00:20:35.818 --> 00:20:37.987
[Niccolò] Move! Move! Move!

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:10.477
Were you frightened earlier?

00:21:11.979 --> 00:21:13.815
I was not.

00:21:15.191 --> 00:21:18.527
I was terrified
the first time I left home.

00:21:20.612 --> 00:21:24.075
Venezia was all I had ever known.

00:21:24.158 --> 00:21:26.160
Do you know how I persevered?

00:21:28.871 --> 00:21:32.083
Knowing just where home was...

00:21:32.166 --> 00:21:35.044
and that I could always return to it.

00:21:40.842 --> 00:21:43.094
Do you see those stars there?

00:21:45.387 --> 00:21:48.265
The Three Sisters.

00:21:50.267 --> 00:21:52.937
The Three Sisters.

00:21:59.026 --> 00:22:01.070
If you are ever afraid...

00:22:02.905 --> 00:22:05.199
if ever you doubt
your place in the world...

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.455
follow The Three Sisters
and they will lead you home.

00:22:17.753 --> 00:22:18.963
My only fear...

00:22:20.047 --> 00:22:22.674
is that I might awaken in my bed...

00:22:22.758 --> 00:22:26.262
destined to live a common life once again.

00:22:27.721 --> 00:22:30.391
The blood of an adventurer
courses through your veins.

00:22:30.474 --> 00:22:32.351
I can see this.

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.943
You will enjoy
the greatest adventure of all.

00:22:42.194 --> 00:22:43.195
You will meet...

00:22:43.279 --> 00:22:46.240
the richest...

00:22:46.323 --> 00:22:50.786
most powerful king
on the face of this earth.

00:22:51.828 --> 00:22:54.957
The Great Kublai Khan.

00:23:16.895 --> 00:23:18.689
[Kublai] The Song rebels of Xiangyang...

00:23:18.772 --> 00:23:22.776
can no longer cast aside our dominion
with impunity.

00:23:22.859 --> 00:23:27.281
As my trusted advisors,
I seek your counsel.

00:23:27.364 --> 00:23:29.075
Jingim.

00:23:32.286 --> 00:23:34.121
You will one day sit here where I do now.

00:23:34.205 --> 00:23:37.458
Speak to your uncles
and cousins who have traveled far.

00:23:40.461 --> 00:23:44.131
Destroying the
Song dynasty rebels is wise.

00:23:44.215 --> 00:23:47.093
But is it not wiser to let them
remain in their Walled City...

00:23:47.176 --> 00:23:49.971
paying us tribute?

00:23:50.054 --> 00:23:53.557
What does my vice regent, Yusuf,
say on this matter?

00:23:55.101 --> 00:23:56.852
Prince Jingim is correct.

00:23:56.935 --> 00:23:58.354
[grunts]

00:23:58.437 --> 00:24:01.357
North China already adores Lord Kublai.

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:04.526
Let South China remain
within their Walled City.

00:24:05.569 --> 00:24:06.945
Treat the rebels as a...

00:24:07.029 --> 00:24:09.615
cow that we draw milk from...

00:24:09.698 --> 00:24:13.744
rather than slaughtering the cow,
and receiving no milk.

00:24:14.745 --> 00:24:15.954
[Ahmad] Or silk...

00:24:16.038 --> 00:24:17.664
in this case.

00:24:21.877 --> 00:24:25.589
The Walled City of Xiangyang...
guards the Yangtze River.

00:24:25.672 --> 00:24:28.175
And the Yangtze
is the gateway to all China.

00:24:28.259 --> 00:24:30.761
You are the Great Khan of Khans.

00:24:30.844 --> 00:24:35.891
You desire a unified China.
It should be yours no matter the cost.

00:24:35.974 --> 00:24:38.019
The Minister of Finance speaks well.

00:24:39.061 --> 00:24:40.979
But this is a matter of
security and defense,

00:24:41.063 --> 00:24:43.149
not coin and commerce.

00:24:43.232 --> 00:24:45.026
[Ariq] Hmm...

00:24:49.363 --> 00:24:51.698
Little brother...

00:24:51.782 --> 00:24:53.367
Ariq the Strong.

00:24:54.618 --> 00:24:57.121
How are things in Karakorum?

00:24:57.204 --> 00:24:58.455
Things in the Old Capital

00:24:58.539 --> 00:25:01.583
are just as our grandfather, Genghis,
would have them.

00:25:01.667 --> 00:25:02.709
[Kublai] Hmm.

00:25:02.793 --> 00:25:04.586
[Ariq] But there are some
in Karakorum who fear

00:25:04.670 --> 00:25:09.091
that our Khan is becoming too Chinese...
too cultured in his ways.

00:25:12.094 --> 00:25:13.220
[Kaidu] Lord Khan...

00:25:14.221 --> 00:25:17.474
may your western cousins
from the House of Ögödei speak?

00:25:20.394 --> 00:25:23.605
Does the Great Khan desire
to be Emperor of Mongolia...

00:25:25.149 --> 00:25:26.692
or Emperor of China?

00:25:29.445 --> 00:25:30.779
[chuckles]

00:25:37.328 --> 00:25:38.870
Cousin Kaidu...

00:25:41.248 --> 00:25:44.418
you forget the mandate
Grandfather was handed from heaven.

00:25:45.586 --> 00:25:49.215
To erase dividing lines
from country to country.

00:25:49.298 --> 00:25:52.259
A mandate to spread our customs...

00:25:52.343 --> 00:25:55.679
our cultures...
our very way of life...

00:25:55.762 --> 00:25:58.432
to every corner beneath the Blue Sky.

00:25:59.433 --> 00:26:03.437
Only one thing stood in his way,
as it now stands in mine.

00:26:04.980 --> 00:26:08.066
Xiangyang... the Walled City.

00:26:08.150 --> 00:26:10.611
I have already sent troops
into South China.

00:26:10.694 --> 00:26:12.696
They are amassing at this very moment.

00:26:12.779 --> 00:26:16.783
My spies tell me that in order to
starve the rebels out...

00:26:16.867 --> 00:26:20.204
we must cut them off
from the farming village of Wuchang.

00:26:20.287 --> 00:26:24.125
I am sending horse soldiers
to that position.

00:26:24.208 --> 00:26:25.417
Jingim...

00:26:26.377 --> 00:26:29.213
blood of my blood,
will lead the assault on Wuchang.

00:26:29.296 --> 00:26:30.381
[Kaidu] Jingim...

00:26:30.464 --> 00:26:33.049
educated in Chinese ways.

00:26:33.967 --> 00:26:36.262
Who better to lead
an attack on the Chinese?

00:26:37.179 --> 00:26:39.140
[Ariq] Older brother...

00:26:39.223 --> 00:26:43.477
if this is a call to war...
you will have my horse and bow.

00:26:43.560 --> 00:26:46.647
I will lead our Golden Horde
down from the north...

00:26:46.730 --> 00:26:49.358
and into battle with my nephew.

00:26:49.441 --> 00:26:53.320
We will crush Wuchang,
then take the Walled City.

00:26:54.696 --> 00:26:56.740
And by the blood of Genghis...

00:26:56.823 --> 00:27:01.203
I will cut their leader's head off
and tie it to the mane of my horse!

00:27:01.287 --> 00:27:02.621
[Kublai chuckling]

00:27:04.456 --> 00:27:06.417
Emperor of China?

00:27:07.793 --> 00:27:09.085
Emperor of Mongolia?

00:27:10.212 --> 00:27:11.880
I will be Emperor of the World!

00:27:42.786 --> 00:27:44.746
[Jia Sidao] Empress Dowager.

00:27:46.790 --> 00:27:47.874
Rise.

00:27:50.168 --> 00:27:52.796
How may the Chancellor ease your pain?

00:27:52.879 --> 00:27:56.425
Tell me the barbarians
are no longer marching toward us.

00:27:57.593 --> 00:28:00.221
[Jia Sidao] I will not lie.
The Khan's troops advance.

00:28:01.012 --> 00:28:02.848
But upon the soul of our Emperor...

00:28:02.931 --> 00:28:05.476
I promise, they will never succeed.

00:28:09.062 --> 00:28:11.732
Long live Song empire.

00:28:21.367 --> 00:28:25.704
My mantis is great.
Do you see?

00:28:25.787 --> 00:28:30.501
He feigns inferiority
to encourage his opponent's advance.

00:28:32.336 --> 00:28:34.296
[Jia Sidao]
I paid a visit to the Emperor's bedside.

00:28:34.380 --> 00:28:35.839
[Red Brow]
How is he?

00:28:35.922 --> 00:28:37.883
Quite unwell.

00:28:39.718 --> 00:28:43.847
[Red Brow] His legacy will live on
within these walls.

00:28:43.930 --> 00:28:47.934
It will be a sad day...
but much more efficient once he's gone.

00:28:49.185 --> 00:28:52.063
No more mixed messages
from an old king to his people.

00:28:52.147 --> 00:28:55.442
I will give all orders
and all orders will be followed.

00:28:55.526 --> 00:28:58.069
Yes, my Chancellor.

00:28:58.153 --> 00:29:01.072
And that goes for
the Emperor's favorite royal concubine.

00:29:02.324 --> 00:29:03.825
Where is your sister?

00:29:03.909 --> 00:29:06.370
Doing that for which she is famous.

00:29:06.453 --> 00:29:10.707
Improving diplomatic ties
with the Governor of Suzhou.

00:29:13.126 --> 00:29:14.753
[breathing heavily]

00:29:14.836 --> 00:29:16.672
Do you know this game?

00:29:19.300 --> 00:29:23.219
[Mei Lin] How much did you
pay my brother for this opportunity?

00:29:23.304 --> 00:29:27.015
More porcelain than he's ever seen.

00:29:35.148 --> 00:29:36.942
Do not fear, Governor.

00:29:37.734 --> 00:29:40.446
This is part of the game you paid for.

00:29:40.529 --> 00:29:44.157
-The Danger Game.
-[whimpers]

00:29:44.240 --> 00:29:46.285
You...

00:29:46.368 --> 00:29:50.121
are but a lowly... worm.

00:29:53.041 --> 00:29:55.961
[panting]

00:30:27.868 --> 00:30:29.119
[door opens]

00:30:31.162 --> 00:30:32.373
[guard] Come.

00:31:00.692 --> 00:31:03.194
[Hundred Eyes]
You have questions.

00:31:03.278 --> 00:31:04.738
[Marco] Just one.

00:31:04.821 --> 00:31:07.240
Am I a privileged guest
or a prisoner in this hell?

00:31:07.323 --> 00:31:08.534
[Hundred Eyes chuckles]

00:31:08.617 --> 00:31:10.035
A fiery one.

00:31:10.118 --> 00:31:13.872
No wonder the Khan caged you
for his own personal amusement.

00:31:17.959 --> 00:31:19.085
You're blind.

00:31:20.253 --> 00:31:22.005
Not as blind as you, boy.

00:31:31.473 --> 00:31:33.141
No roots.

00:31:35.894 --> 00:31:37.813
You have spirit, Latin.

00:31:37.896 --> 00:31:40.899
Of the Yin and the Yang,
you have an abundance of Yang.

00:31:41.817 --> 00:31:43.944
But without Yin,
Yang dies on the battlefield.

00:31:45.111 --> 00:31:47.280
We are all prisoners here.

00:31:47.363 --> 00:31:51.452
Prisoners and privileged guests.
One and the same.

00:31:52.536 --> 00:31:55.872
If you are unable to protect yourself
in the kingdom...

00:31:55.956 --> 00:31:58.750
it is I... who will be killed.

00:32:00.376 --> 00:32:02.087
Do you understand?

00:32:03.338 --> 00:32:06.132
Good. We begin with roots.

00:32:11.221 --> 00:32:15.476
[Hundred Eyes] <i>You have been conscripted</i>
<i>into the court of Kublai Khan.</i>

00:32:15.559 --> 00:32:17.185
<i>For what? I do not know.</i>

00:32:18.269 --> 00:32:20.146
<i>-I am Hundred Eyes.</i>
-[grunting]

00:32:20.230 --> 00:32:23.859
<i>I am kept here to train the Khan's sons...</i>
<i>his nobles...</i>

00:32:25.026 --> 00:32:26.695
<i>his pets.</i>

00:32:26.778 --> 00:32:28.029
[neighing]

00:32:28.113 --> 00:32:31.241
<i>You shall be tutored</i>
<i>in the Mongolian ways of the horse.</i>

00:32:31.324 --> 00:32:34.578
[children shouting in foreign language]

00:32:37.372 --> 00:32:39.833
<i>You shall be tutored</i>
<i>in the great arts of the East...</i>

00:32:39.916 --> 00:32:44.254
<i>by those scholars and artisans</i>
<i>loyal to Lord Kublai.</i>

00:32:45.171 --> 00:32:47.508
<i>Languages and letters.</i>

00:32:47.591 --> 00:32:50.051
<i>Hawking and archery.</i>

00:32:50.135 --> 00:32:55.015
<i>And in the end... you may discover</i>
<i>the answer to your question.</i>

00:32:56.933 --> 00:32:58.393
[door opens]

00:33:19.915 --> 00:33:22.959
[man pleading in foreign language]

00:33:33.053 --> 00:33:35.681
[Kublai] A man found in possession
of a stolen horse...

00:33:35.764 --> 00:33:39.976
must return it to its owner,
add nine horses of the same kind.

00:33:40.060 --> 00:33:42.437
If he is unable to pay this fine...

00:33:42.521 --> 00:33:45.356
his children must be
taken instead of the horses.

00:33:45.440 --> 00:33:47.275
If he has no children...

00:33:47.358 --> 00:33:49.736
then he must be
slaughtered like a sheep.

00:33:49.820 --> 00:33:52.155
That man has no children.

00:33:53.990 --> 00:33:58.453
I hear from my Minister of Falconry,
you have taken well to the hawks.

00:33:58.537 --> 00:34:00.371
Archery is improving, yes?

00:34:00.455 --> 00:34:02.498
Yes, Great Khan.

00:34:02.583 --> 00:34:07.337
I, myself, was always a bit clumsy
with the making of Chinese characters.

00:34:09.339 --> 00:34:11.883
When you and your father
crossed Central Asia...

00:34:11.967 --> 00:34:13.594
you passed through Badakhshān.

00:34:13.677 --> 00:34:17.430
Describe for me,
in the way that you do...

00:34:17.513 --> 00:34:20.934
how you made the passage,
what you saw.

00:34:22.352 --> 00:34:23.645
We saw sand.

00:34:25.188 --> 00:34:27.023
Rode beasts.

00:34:28.900 --> 00:34:30.318
Do you defy me?

00:34:31.820 --> 00:34:34.364
Describe for me
the land of Badakhshān.

00:34:35.531 --> 00:34:38.201
The footing was hard on our beasts.

00:34:38.284 --> 00:34:39.452
The sun very hot.

00:34:39.535 --> 00:34:42.748
Take him to the horse grounds.
Stuff his mouth with the shit of pigs.

00:34:42.831 --> 00:34:44.833
You enter a gate made of rock...

00:34:44.916 --> 00:34:46.918
east of Bukhara...

00:34:47.002 --> 00:34:49.295
and begin to ascend
into the Pamir Mountains.

00:34:52.924 --> 00:34:55.927
There are great numbers
of all kind of wild beasts.

00:34:56.011 --> 00:34:57.178
And the men of Badakhshān...

00:34:57.262 --> 00:35:01.349
speak of a breed of horse which is said
to be the direct offspring of Alexander's.

00:35:04.269 --> 00:35:05.353
[Kublai grunts]

00:35:06.521 --> 00:35:09.065
Odd bit of trivia.

00:35:09.149 --> 00:35:12.736
I've always been taken
by the audacity of Alexander.

00:35:12.819 --> 00:35:14.655
A great conqueror.

00:35:14.738 --> 00:35:17.323
There are 20 cities
that bear his name, huh?

00:35:18.617 --> 00:35:20.827
I now possess them all.

00:35:22.578 --> 00:35:25.331
Do you blame me
for your current station in life?

00:35:25.415 --> 00:35:26.667
No, Sire.

00:35:28.293 --> 00:35:30.336
I simply wonder why you kept me.

00:35:30.420 --> 00:35:33.548
I need no reason, Latin.

00:35:37.010 --> 00:35:38.594
As my servant...

00:35:38.679 --> 00:35:41.765
you will accompany a tax collector
as he makes his rounds.

00:35:41.848 --> 00:35:45.518
This will give you a view of my
Imperial City and my subjects.

00:35:45.601 --> 00:35:47.688
You will report back to me,
describe what you have seen...

00:35:47.771 --> 00:35:49.522
as you saw it.

00:35:51.024 --> 00:35:52.984
I'm giving you freedom.

00:35:55.737 --> 00:35:58.489
But the walls of my kingdom
stretch beyond the horizon.

00:35:58.573 --> 00:36:00.158
Do you understand?

00:36:01.201 --> 00:36:02.869
Yes, Sire.

00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:05.789
I give you leave.

00:36:05.872 --> 00:36:07.165
Hmm?

00:36:21.012 --> 00:36:24.390
I assumed you would be
riding to Wuchang by now.

00:36:24.474 --> 00:36:28.186
The astrologers told you this morning
was the most auspicious hour to march.

00:36:28.269 --> 00:36:31.647
The Confucian advisors said
it is better we ride at night.

00:36:31.732 --> 00:36:33.066
Ugh.

00:36:33.149 --> 00:36:36.695
They also believe
a war can be won without fighting.

00:36:36.778 --> 00:36:39.489
Why must they always speak in riddles?

00:36:39.572 --> 00:36:42.408
-"The supreme art of war," Father.
-Mmm.

00:36:43.744 --> 00:36:45.078
Still...

00:36:46.037 --> 00:36:48.790
tomorrow I ride to
Wuchang as a Mongol...

00:36:48.874 --> 00:36:51.126
and I carry my father's flag.

00:36:52.043 --> 00:36:54.045
You are your mother's son, Jingim.

00:36:54.963 --> 00:36:57.883
Educated... patient... noble.

00:36:57.966 --> 00:37:01.720
There will be a time
for all these things in the new dynasty.

00:37:03.429 --> 00:37:05.556
I must prepare to ride.

00:37:05.640 --> 00:37:09.602
My three wives each desire a visit
before I go to battle.

00:37:09.685 --> 00:37:11.604
[laughing]

00:37:11.687 --> 00:37:13.606
You're also your father's son.

00:37:23.491 --> 00:37:24.785
[both panting]

00:37:25.827 --> 00:37:30.206
Give to me the nectar...
so I keep it when you go...

00:37:30.290 --> 00:37:31.958
and give you a son.

00:37:35.045 --> 00:37:37.463
-And what if it's a daughter?
-[chuckles]

00:37:38.757 --> 00:37:43.261
Yang the Healer says to do it like this,
in the Golden Lotus,

00:37:43.344 --> 00:37:45.931
and I shall finally bear you an heir.

00:37:48.892 --> 00:37:51.602
Yang the Healer
will be promoted to the ministry.

00:37:51.686 --> 00:37:53.104
[both laughing]

00:37:55.648 --> 00:37:57.108
Tell me...

00:37:57.192 --> 00:38:00.195
does your Chinese wife
do it like this? Huh?

00:38:01.321 --> 00:38:02.488
[Jingim] Shh.

00:38:02.572 --> 00:38:03.907
[both panting]

00:38:11.122 --> 00:38:12.457
[horses approaching]

00:39:22.903 --> 00:39:24.445
[indistinct chatter]

00:39:33.121 --> 00:39:34.539
[people clapping]

00:39:36.832 --> 00:39:41.171
[woman] Nice. They're so beautiful.
You can let it go.

00:39:42.088 --> 00:39:44.340
Are you ready?

00:39:44.424 --> 00:39:46.176
Here we go.

00:39:48.761 --> 00:39:51.556
-[gasping]
-[laughter]

00:39:51.639 --> 00:39:53.766
[applause]

00:40:00.606 --> 00:40:01.816
Ah...

00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:03.568
the Venetian.

00:40:03.651 --> 00:40:06.947
A pleasure to formally
make your acquaintance.

00:40:11.701 --> 00:40:14.955
She is my charge, so avert your gaze.

00:40:16.831 --> 00:40:20.751
She is far past the reach
of a foreign merchant's son.

00:40:21.962 --> 00:40:23.713
I followed the wrong path.

00:40:23.796 --> 00:40:25.798
-Indeed you did...
-[bell tolls]

00:40:27.008 --> 00:40:30.845
and the clock tower
just struck first bell.

00:40:30.929 --> 00:40:32.763
My apologies to you.

00:40:56.121 --> 00:41:00.333
The Governor said the songs they sing
about you south of Quinsai are true.

00:41:00.416 --> 00:41:01.876
You pleased him greatly.

00:41:03.128 --> 00:41:04.504
[Mei Lin]
The Emperor's dying.

00:41:04.587 --> 00:41:06.881
You must honor his wishes.

00:41:06.965 --> 00:41:08.549
Anything he wants.

00:41:08.633 --> 00:41:10.010
Make a truce with the barbarians.

00:41:10.093 --> 00:41:13.972
That was not what the Emperor desired
when he was well and strong.

00:41:14.055 --> 00:41:18.059
Truce is the dying cry
of the weak and the sick.

00:41:18.143 --> 00:41:19.644
[Mei Lin]
Kublai is too strong.

00:41:19.727 --> 00:41:22.688
I worry for my daughter
if the barbarians take our city.

00:41:22.772 --> 00:41:25.400
Let your Chancellor
manage military affairs.

00:41:25.483 --> 00:41:27.943
You manage the imperial bed chamber.

00:41:29.362 --> 00:41:33.408
Let the Chancellor not forget who it was
who won him favor in this court.

00:41:35.201 --> 00:41:39.164
When the strike of the praying mantis
breaks the body of the cricket,

00:41:39.247 --> 00:41:40.999
it is because of its timing.

00:41:41.082 --> 00:41:43.251
Timing, Mei Lin.

00:41:43.334 --> 00:41:46.671
Trust me, like my soldiers do.

00:41:49.215 --> 00:41:51.842
And worry no more.

00:41:51.926 --> 00:41:56.847
When the Emperor is gone,
you will still be esteemed in this court.

00:42:07.692 --> 00:42:08.943
[grunts]

00:42:09.027 --> 00:42:10.153
[Hundred Eyes]
Get up.

00:42:12.155 --> 00:42:13.531
Get up.

00:42:20.205 --> 00:42:21.997
I did not ask to train you, Latin.

00:42:22.082 --> 00:42:24.084
There is no honor in this for me.

00:42:27.420 --> 00:42:29.672
Nor did you ask
to be left here by a man

00:42:29.755 --> 00:42:33.218
who would trade his own son
like 2 pounds of spice...

00:42:36.721 --> 00:42:40.933
for the opportunity
to open trade routes to the West.

00:42:47.273 --> 00:42:49.234
Go ahead, take it.

00:43:03.831 --> 00:43:05.083
Let him go, Latin.

00:43:05.958 --> 00:43:07.335
Let him go.

00:43:18.638 --> 00:43:20.098
Get up.

00:43:22.142 --> 00:43:25.186
If you wish to survive here,
get up at once.

00:43:34.028 --> 00:43:36.531
The foreigner has been summoned.

00:43:42.745 --> 00:43:44.664
It is quiet.

00:43:44.747 --> 00:43:46.957
As it is before a typhoon.

00:43:51.879 --> 00:43:55.466
By the Eternal Blue Sky,
let us sing from our throats

00:43:55.550 --> 00:43:58.344
and let them hear the devil
that they are about to meet.

00:43:58.428 --> 00:44:02.640
The sons of my father's concubines
always speak the loudest.

00:44:04.350 --> 00:44:06.686
We must attack as Genghis would.

00:44:09.522 --> 00:44:11.732
Ariq... he is not there.

00:44:11.816 --> 00:44:14.068
What do you mean
"he is not there"?

00:44:14.152 --> 00:44:15.986
[panting] No Ariq.

00:44:16.070 --> 00:44:17.780
No Golden Horde.

00:44:17.863 --> 00:44:20.408
Just grass and sky.

00:44:33.003 --> 00:44:34.339
[Nima] Ah, yes.

00:44:34.422 --> 00:44:35.965
Welcome.

00:44:36.882 --> 00:44:38.634
Proceed down the hall.

00:44:40.553 --> 00:44:44.349
And Master Marco...
I will be watching you.

00:44:56.694 --> 00:44:58.446
[women moaning]

00:45:06.329 --> 00:45:07.580
[women giggling]

00:45:27.016 --> 00:45:28.142
[Kublai] Enter.

00:45:31.854 --> 00:45:33.022
Sire.

00:45:34.565 --> 00:45:38.235
Your new quarters are more
spacious than the last, no?

00:45:38.319 --> 00:45:41.406
Yes, very much. Thank you.

00:45:45.951 --> 00:45:48.162
[Kublai]
I have a test for you.

00:45:48.245 --> 00:45:51.206
You will walk back down
the Hall of Five Desires.

00:45:51.291 --> 00:45:52.792
These girls are from Kungurat...

00:45:53.793 --> 00:45:56.796
highly skilled in the arts of love.

00:45:57.797 --> 00:46:03.093
A man who proves his loyalty to me
can take whatever he wishes.

00:46:03.177 --> 00:46:05.305
-You may not.
-[women moaning]

00:46:05.388 --> 00:46:06.681
Not yet.

00:46:09.141 --> 00:46:13.145
Look... but do not touch.

00:46:25.533 --> 00:46:28.703
[Chabi] The walls have eyes, Marco Polo.

00:46:41.507 --> 00:46:42.800
[women moaning]

00:47:21.881 --> 00:47:25.092
[distant chanting]

00:47:26.386 --> 00:47:28.929
Do you hear them taunt us?

00:47:29.013 --> 00:47:31.516
They mock our blood.

00:47:31.599 --> 00:47:35.645
Even without Ariq's army,
we should still attack like Mongols...

00:47:35.728 --> 00:47:38.147
or retreat as cowards.

00:47:39.815 --> 00:47:41.567
[Jingim] That is no farming village.

00:47:42.610 --> 00:47:44.820
How many men did you say we have?

00:47:44.904 --> 00:47:46.363
Five hundred?

00:47:48.449 --> 00:47:50.325
And down there?

00:47:50.410 --> 00:47:53.203
[Byamba]
More. Many more.

00:47:53.287 --> 00:47:54.539
[Aruka] As your General...

00:47:55.330 --> 00:47:58.375
I advise... retreat.

00:48:13.724 --> 00:48:16.977
We do not return home
until we conquer that village.

00:48:20.314 --> 00:48:21.482
Give the command.

00:48:33.703 --> 00:48:35.162
[yelling]

00:48:37.164 --> 00:48:39.166
[theme music playing]